From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:42:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: no full-screen console check

Windows 10 Mobile's kernel32 has no GetConsoleDisplayMode, and Chrome's
browser layer brings in IsFullScreenConsoleMode (presentation-mode
detection for notifications), whose load-time import of it kept the
engine DLL from loading at all (LoadPackagedLibrary error 127, the
shell's import probe naming it). There are no consoles on a phone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ui/base/fullscreen_win.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/base/fullscreen_win.cc b/ui/base/fullscreen_win.cc
index 5a18bd1618869ae94a9eb1563e3245bb57f47e6c..d85eb9e0e9f7e5b39c8a79ee7b5f2a74db6903e2 100644
--- a/ui/base/fullscreen_win.cc
+++ b/ui/base/fullscreen_win.cc
@@ -56,6 +56,12 @@ bool IsFullScreenWindowMode() {
 }
 
 bool IsFullScreenConsoleMode() {
+#if defined(VENETIUM_W10M)
+  // No consoles on Windows 10 Mobile, whose kernel32 has no
+  // GetConsoleDisplayMode either: imported, it kept the engine DLL from
+  // loading at all.
+  return false;
+#else
   // We detect this by attaching the current process to the console of the
   // foreground window and then checking if it is in full screen mode.
   DWORD pid = 0;
@@ -71,6 +77,7 @@ bool IsFullScreenConsoleMode() {
   ::FreeConsole();
 
   return (modes & (CONSOLE_FULLSCREEN | CONSOLE_FULLSCREEN_HARDWARE)) != 0;
+#endif  // defined(VENETIUM_W10M)
 }
 
 }  // namespace
